🚨 **BLOCKING: Superseded by #1081 (already merged into `main`) — branch also conflicts**

PR #1081 (commit `83d68f305`, merged 2026-09-29 23:22 UTC) fixes this exact site with the identical change:

```dart
// dart2js: shifts are 32-bit — `1 << 32` == 0, so nextInt(0) would throw
// on web and kill every bash call (issue #1074). Spell the bound literally.
final rand = _shellJobRandom.nextInt(0xFFFFFFFF).toRadixString(36);
```

and likewise fixes all other four sites in this PR (`generate_image.dart`, `generate_video.dart`, `agent_message.dart`, `session_lease.dart`), so merging this PR changes only comment wording. #1081 additionally covers what this PR defers to follow-up: the sentinel shifts (`1 << 62` / `1 << 60` / `1 << 40` / `1 << 31`), the `nextFrameId` `(hi << 16) | lo` recombine hazard in `bridge_protocol.dart`, the source-scan guard `test/dart2js_shift_guard_test.dart`, and a `newShellJobId` unit test.

Independently, this branch no longer merges: `git merge-tree` against `origin/main` (`69ca888e0`) reports conflicts in **all 5 files this PR touches**, each exactly in these hunks — confirmed by the existing PR thread warning at head `f15126ba4`. Branch base is `1611339ef`; `main` has moved 7 commits ahead since.

**Recommendation**: close this PR in favor of #1081; no rework needed. (The fix technique itself — a literal bound instead of `1 << 32` — is correct and matches what merged.)

